# Match at any depth: the workspace shares /target, but the workspace-excluded
# crates (fuzz, justerm-facade, justerm-renderer) each build their own target/ dir (#100).
target/

# wasm-pack build output (the npm artifact is built in CI / on publish, never committed).
# wasm-pack also writes a nested .gitignore in each, but make it explicit here too.
/justerm-wasm-decode/pkg*

# Local scratch (personal prompt notes — not part of the crate)
/prompt.md

# justerm-web (TS package) — deps + build output, never committed.
/justerm-web/node_modules
/justerm-web/dist

# Playwright MCP live-drive artifacts (snapshots/console logs — scratch, not committed).
.playwright-mcp/

# Clean-room verification of a PUBLISHED package (`npm pack` + unpack, to judge what a
# consumer actually receives). Scratch by construction: it holds a tarball and its unpacked
# tree at whatever version was current that day, so it goes stale the next release and is one
# `npm pack` away from being rebuilt. Named here rather than left untracked because it was
# not: a 0.10.0 renderer tarball, wasm binary included, sat in `git status` as `??` for two
# days against a shipped 0.11.0, one `git add -A` away from being committed.
/jrcheck/

# thegraph run state (docs/agents/thegraph.md § Run state). A cache during the run;
# the issue is the durable record. A cache that reaches a review is noise.
/.thegraph/
